<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Banu Kanz emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1004 CE – 1412 CE (approx.) · capital Aswan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Arab-Nubian dynasty of Aswan that guarded Egypt's southern frontier and eventually claimed the throne of Makuria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kanz">Banu Kanz</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabia">Rabi'a</a> tribe who settled in the Aswan region and the gold mines of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-desert">Eastern Desert</a> in the 9th century and intermarried with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubians">Nubians</a> and Beja. In 1006 the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Hakim gave their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-makarim-hibat-allah">Abu al-Makarim Hibat Allah</a> the title Kanz al-Dawla for capturing the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-rakwa">Abu Rakwa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Kanz al-Dawla chiefs ruled the southern marches around Aswan as hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, controlling trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> and the gold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadi-allaqi">Wadi Allaqi</a>. In 1174 they rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> and were crushed. Moving southwards, they grew close to the Makurian royal family, and in 1317 to 1323 a Kanzi prince, Kanz al-Dawla, ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/makuria">Makuria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kanz">Banu Kanz</a> helped spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and Arabic among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubians">Nubians</a> but clashed repeatedly with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, which broke their power around 1412. Their name survives in the Kenzi Nubians of the Aswan region.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1004 CE – 1412 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.68%;width:8.12%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1004 CE – 1412 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aswan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu al-Makarim Hibat Allah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Nubian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu Kanz, Kanz al-Dawla, Emirate of Aswan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=banu-kanz-emirate" aria-label="Banu Kanz emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5556 1290 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banu Kanz emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5876 1546L5811 1337M5876 1546L5815 1335M5876 1546L5833 1758"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M5815 1335h0M5833 1758h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5876 1546h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5876 1546h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aswan. <a href="/atlas?